memory_endpoints_two_use_context:
  - Direct use: ecosystem agents use MemoryEndpoints.com for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across all sites.
  - Separate plugin use: a TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - Lane boundary: keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate; neither lane silently acts for the other.

single_tinyrustlm_source_prohibitions:
  - Do not create, adopt, maintain, edit, build, test, release, deploy, or describe more than one authoritative TinyRustLM.com source checkout.
  - The sole local TinyRustLM.com source root is E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com; fail closed if that path is absent, points through a reparse point, is not the declared remote-exact worktree, or any recovered, dated, hidden, backup, Worktrees, or quarantine source copy exists.
  - Do not treat a clone, copied directory, recovery tree, Git worktree, generated package, deployed web root, backup, evidence root, or protected damaged snapshot as a second source authority.
  - Before any TinyRustLM.com work, resolve the canonical root from its current workspace.uai and verify the canonical path, branch, origin URL, local HEAD, tracking ref, FETCH_HEAD, direct remote ref, and worktree status; do not edit while identity is ambiguous.
  - Fail closed before editing, building, testing, committing, releasing, or deploying when canonical authority cannot be proved or any second writable TinyRustLM.com checkout is discovered; consolidation and retirement must finish before work resumes.
  - Every workspace registry, read order, build recipe, CI workflow, release command, and deployment manifest must name only the canonical authority; automated gates must reject pointers to duplicate, retired, quarantined, protected, or otherwise non-authoritative source.
  - Any committed change to a declared public artifact invalidates deployed-current status until a strictly newer release is published from one clean canonical commit, every declared readable file passes byte-for-byte HTTPS readback, every retired route is absent, and the public release records agree. Never mask drift with stale metadata, a partial upload, an overwrite under an old version, or source-only success.
  - Do not create temporary scratch or test Git worktrees, repository clones, or copied ecosystem source trees anywhere. Tests may create only operation-owned, bounded, non-product, non-source fixtures; they must contain no Git metadata or workspace/taboo authority markers, must never deploy, and must be physically removed when their operation closes.
  - If duplication or divergence appears, make no new edits in the duplicate. Inventory its commits and local diff, move only valid current clean-slate work into the canonical tree, reject legacy, compatibility, fallback, and debt, run every affected gate, commit and push the canonical tree, and then retire the duplicate safely.
  - Do not pull both trees forward, merge stale branches wholesale, preserve a second checkout as history, or keep obsolete executable code, schemas, routes, docs, or configuration active. Historical source belongs only in Git history; bounded evidence may describe it but must not execute or compete with current authority.

ecosystem_source_root_prohibitions:
  - The only local editable source roots for this ecosystem are the seven direct repositories E:\Source\Rust\LMComposer.com, E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.MiRust.com, E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org, E:\Source\Rust\MiRust.com, E:\Source\Rust\Runtime.MiRust.com, E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com, and E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.MiRust.com.
  - Do not retain another ecosystem source checkout, copied source tree, Git metadata clone, archive, recovery root, worktree, quarantine, proof clone, or loose source/config copy inside any registered governed root. A second copy found there, or at any other known source-bearing location, is a blocking defect even when labeled temporary, retired, stale, protected, evidence, or backup.
  - Source-producing recovery, build, test, packaging, demo, and deployment tooling must resolve one of the seven canonical repository roots before reading editable source and must fail closed before writing source, Git metadata, workspace authority, or editable configuration anywhere else. Owned temporary roots may contain only bounded non-source outputs, must carry an operation-specific ownership marker, and must be physically removed when their operation closes.
  - The enforceable discovery boundary is the seven canonical repositories; the recursively registered E:\Source\Rust, E:\Source\Worktrees, E:\Source\.codex-tmp, E:\Source\.codex-temp, E:\Source\.tinyrustlm-evidence, and E:\Source\External scopes; every ecosystem-shaped direct E:\Source child; a direct-root plus one-child marker probe for every other neutral direct E:\Source child; and D:\tw, D:\Archive\Source, and D:\TinyRustLM-vnext-20260812 at their declared bounded depths. A passing gate proves only those boundaries; it is not a whole-volume inventory of E: or D: and does not recursively inspect unrelated sibling repositories. Register and completely scan any newly known or suspected source-bearing location, or physically retire it, before claiming sole-source authority.
  - Deployment bundles and immutable private evidence may retain only bounded non-authoritative artifacts. They must not contain Git metadata, an authoritative workspace.uai plus .uai/taboo.uai pair, editable product source, or build, test, commit, release, or deployment entrypoints.
  - Before any ecosystem edit, build, or test, run E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com\tinyrustlm\tools\verify-single-source-authority.js from the canonical TinyRustLM.com root. Require Windows, the exact direct non-reparse E:\Source\Rust layout, exact Git top-levels, branches, and sole fetch/push origins, every registered superseded path absent, every source-marker read successful inside a governed scan or neutral direct-child probe, every recursively registered scan complete and readable, and exactly the seven declared roots. Unsupported layout, unreadable governed metadata, damaged Git markers, or incomplete governed enumeration is failure, never an implicit pass.
  - The only permitted ecosystem source-authority marker files are the root workspace.uai and root .uai/taboo.uai of the seven declared canonical repositories. The source-authority gate must recursively scan every registered E:\Source scope, including non-repository children of E:\Source\Rust, directly probe neutral sibling roots without entering unrelated nested test or repository storage, and scan D:\tw to depth 3, D:\Archive\Source to depth 3, D:\TinyRustLM-vnext-20260812 to depth 32, and E:\Source\External\TinyRustLM-release-evidence to depth 5; reject every other source root found at those boundaries, loose Git/source/config file in a recursively governed scope, nested or packaged workspace.uai or .uai/taboo.uai, plaintext all-source or source-review bundle, and every TinyRustLM-ecosystem archive candidate except bounded content-inspected, checksum-bound immutable binary-release evidence admitted by this exact policy beneath the registered evidence artifacts/releases or artifacts/browser-packages subtree. Never infer binary evidence from a filename or extension: require bounded archive-byte identity or checksum binding, exact release/SPDX sidecar identities where declared, source-free manifest/member semantics, and treat every unregistered, mismatched, source-bearing, unreadable, noncanonical, depth-limited, or otherwise unscanned governed candidate as blocking or source_authority_scan_incomplete.
  - Before release or deployment, commit and push each coherent repository change from its canonical root, then rerun the verifier with --require-clean --require-remote-exact and require local HEAD, upstream, direct remote branch, tree status, and declared origin to agree. Do not use FETCH_HEAD as authority because it may describe an unrelated fetch.
  - Every forbidden root, loose file, nested or packaged marker, plaintext all-source or source-review bundle, and unregistered or source-bearing archive remains a blocking defect until authorized physical deletion and a fresh complete scan prove absence. Renaming, moving, hiding, quarantining, ACL-protecting, repackaging, or retaining source bytes as evidence does not retire it; bounded evidence may retain identities, inventories, deletion receipts, and exact registered non-source binary/model/build artifacts outside E:\Source\Rust without becoming source authority.
  - Do not create temporary ecosystem source clones or worktrees outside the seven canonical roots. Isolated verification may synthesize only minimal non-product fixtures; each fixture must be operation-owned, bounded, unable to release or deploy, contain no unique product work, and be physically removed when the operation closes. Any surviving source clone, source-bearing fixture, or worktree fails the next source-authority gate.
  - Any committed change to a declared public artifact invalidates deployed-current status until a strictly newer release is published from one clean canonical commit, every declared readable file passes byte-for-byte HTTPS readback, every retired route is absent, and the public release records agree. Never mask drift with stale metadata, a partial upload, an overwrite under an old version, or source-only success.

prohibitions:
  - Do not add or retain legacy readers, compatibility, migrations, aliases, dual protocols, hidden fallback, response repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, low-quality patches, knowingly temporary architecture, or deferred cleanup.
  - Do not infer correctness, numerical parity, quality, browser readiness, P2P availability, memory continuity, deployment, or publication from source, report prose, file size, package creation, fixtures, mocks, local probes, or one attractive response.
  - Do not rerun, repair, adopt, promote, delete, or reinterpret immutable failed operations, including Qwen3 attempt /10.
  - Do not download TXT, JSON, README, PowerShell, or another instruction handoff when a user asks to acquire a model. Import an exact qualified peer composition or perform explicit local conversion.
  - Do not proxy prompts, silently use remote inference, accept arbitrary companion commands/paths/URLs, or publish secrets/private evidence. Under the owner's 2026-09-12 instruction, MiniModel.org may serve the initial verified SLM2 seeds from D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM; TinyRustLM.com continues to serve the browser runtime without model payloads.
  - Do not let documentation, marketing, release logs, versions, source, deployed bytes, or HTTPS readback contradict each other.

memory_endpoints_prohibitions:
  - Do not describe MemoryEndpoints.com as outside the ecosystem plan or deny its authorized two-lane role.
  - Do not conflate direct agent coordination with the TinyRustLM.com Connect user plugin, share credentials across lanes, or let either lane silently act for the other.
  - Do not silently upload prompts, transcripts, local memory, meetings, credentials, invitation URLs, tokens, or raw hosted-memory payloads.
  - Do not claim live communication, account correctness, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity from source code, configuration, reachability, fixtures, or mocks.
  - Do not let redundant prelaunch memory copies drift or silently choose one contradictory copy. Keep each maintained copy current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and reconciled.

evidence_prohibitions:
  - Do not repair raw model output, select a lucky seed, train on holdouts or failed evaluations, inject expected terms, or lower a gate to obtain a pass.
  - Do not call loopback, LAN, hairpin, or local peer checks public proof.
  - Do not call cross-compilation physical execution or package upload publication.
  - Do not increment 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, or 0/20 without exact live receipts.

# User directive 2026-09-12: TinyRustLM storage and replacement policy
# TinyRustLM editable source has one home: E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com.
# TinyRustLM models have one home: D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM; model payloads stay out of Git.
# Never create extra source clones, worktrees, backups, dated copies, proof copies, or scattered tool/build folders.
# Check in coherent source changes regularly; Git history replaces backup source directories.
# Keep bounded temporary build/test output under the canonical repository and remove it when its operation ends.
# When a verified new version replaces an old version, retain only the current copy and remove the superseded bytes.
# Preserve useful unique work in the canonical source or model root before deleting duplicates; keep receipts, not junk copies.
# This explicit user directive supersedes older instructions allowing TinyRustLM source/model sprawl or forbidding the designated D: model store.

# User directive 2026-09-12: retain experiment lessons, not obsolete copies
# Before retiring an experiment, record its purpose, inputs/operation identity, observed outcome, useful lessons, uncertainty, and applicable current tests or code in the owning canonical repository.
# Preserve compact evidence identities and Git references for failed as well as successful experiments; do not preserve copied source trees or superseded models merely as a substitute for recording what was learned.
# Reviewed TinyRustLM and retired-Runtime findings begin at E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com\wiki\runtime-mirust\reports\ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md; this is a growing review, not blanket proof that every experiment has been assessed.
# Training checkpoint replacement must preserve immutable metrics and hash-linked receipts, verify the newest payload before retirement, and keep only one current payload. Never recreate a duplicate final-candidate model directory or treat receipt-only history as loadable weights. Current trainer retention and its verification limits are recorded in lesson T8.
# Do not execute or revive the retired generic sequence/top-k producer chain, old SmolLM2 adapter-source/ALR1 exporter, or their historical recipes. The 26 reviewed source/control files still await owner-run physical retirement after automatic approval review blocked deletion; lessons T9-T11 preserve their useful findings. Source history is in Git 33483be, and only the pinned current working-model lane can obtain fresh training authority.
